WEBVTT

00:08.470 --> 00:09.670
[Running footsteps]

00:09.740 --> 00:13.470
[REINER] Conny! Have you
found any survivors?

00:13.510 --> 00:15.910
--No.
--[REINER and BERTHOLDT gasp]

00:15.940 --> 00:20.450
No. It's, it's in ruins.

00:20.480 --> 00:24.920
My hometown has been
completely wiped out!

00:31.330 --> 00:34.130
[GELGAR]
Hey. Something's wrong.

00:36.300 --> 00:38.970
You find any bodies?

00:39.000 --> 00:40.370
No.

00:40.440 --> 00:42.040
No, not yet.

00:42.100 --> 00:43.770
How is that even possible?

00:43.810 --> 00:46.470
Titans ransack this place and
there's not a speck of blood?

00:46.510 --> 00:47.970
They must've fled.

00:48.010 --> 00:49.780
The villagers, I mean,
they all escaped.

00:49.810 --> 00:52.150
Uh, your family, too.

00:52.180 --> 00:55.050
You think so?
You think they're alive?

00:55.120 --> 00:56.780
Um. Yeah, sure!

00:56.820 --> 00:58.280
It's the only
logical explanation

00:58.320 --> 01:01.720
for why there'd be
no trace of well, carnage.

01:01.790 --> 01:04.620
[GELGAR] I don't know
that I agree with that.

01:04.660 --> 01:08.900
Suppose the entire village
was evacuated in time.

01:08.960 --> 01:11.560
How do you explain
the devastation?

01:11.630 --> 01:15.840
Why would Titans
rip apart empty houses?

01:15.870 --> 01:17.570
And that doesn't
bother me half as much

01:17.640 --> 01:20.810
as the stables being full.

01:20.840 --> 01:24.010
Without horses, the
villagers' odds of survival

01:24.050 --> 01:26.650
are slim to none.

01:26.680 --> 01:28.880
Anyone not have a torch?

01:28.920 --> 01:31.480
Okay. Let's move!

01:31.520 --> 01:33.390
Our mission is
to evaluate the breach!

01:33.420 --> 01:35.490
[REINER]
Sir!

01:44.900 --> 01:48.400
[TITAN 28A]
Huh. Welcome home.

01:48.440 --> 01:53.540
[CONNY exhales quaveringly]

01:53.580 --> 01:56.140
[Exhales]

01:57.110 --> 02:01.910
[Heart beating]

02:01.950 --> 02:05.550
Huh? Did I?

02:05.590 --> 02:07.190
[REINER]
Snap out of it!

02:07.220 --> 02:09.990
We're falling behind
Gelgar and the others!

02:10.060 --> 02:12.260
Do you hear that?
You had to!

02:12.290 --> 02:13.390
I swear that Titan--

02:13.430 --> 02:15.630
It was only
your imagination.

02:15.700 --> 02:19.230
I didn't hear a damn thing.
Focus on the mission.

02:19.270 --> 02:21.630
But, I... It sounded...

02:21.700 --> 02:23.370
I don't know how, but...

02:23.410 --> 02:26.110
It sounded, like my mother.

02:26.140 --> 02:27.670
Dammit, Conny!
Do you even know

02:27.740 --> 02:30.210
how serious our
situation is right now?

02:30.250 --> 02:31.480
If we don't see this through,

02:31.550 --> 02:35.150
people will die in
the hundreds of thousands!

02:35.220 --> 02:36.780
Just 'cause
your family escaped

02:36.820 --> 02:38.990
doesn't mean they're
out of the woods yet!

02:39.050 --> 02:42.090
Now, you wanna be
a soldier or don't you?

02:45.660 --> 02:49.000
Yeah. Stay focused.

02:49.060 --> 02:50.600
[HORSE neighs]

02:50.630 --> 02:52.800
I'm a soldier!

02:57.640 --> 03:02.610
♪ Opening Song

04:37.020 --> 04:38.760
The closer we get
to the wall,

04:38.790 --> 04:41.520
the less populated
the area will be.

04:41.590 --> 04:46.660
That's good. It didn't
take us very long.

04:46.700 --> 04:50.330
All right.
Let's head to the south.

04:50.370 --> 04:51.940
What's the point?

04:51.970 --> 04:55.040
Last I heard there aren't any
villages to the south of here.

04:55.110 --> 04:57.140
We've raised the alarm
for everyone in the region.

04:57.180 --> 04:58.710
Now we pinpoint the breach.

04:58.780 --> 05:02.280
The idea is to ride along the
wall from the west 'til we do.

05:02.310 --> 05:04.010
Seriously?
You know Christa and me

05:04.080 --> 05:05.950
don't have our
battle gear, right?

05:05.980 --> 05:07.720
What're we supposed
to do about Titans?

05:07.790 --> 05:09.450
The south will be
crawlin' with 'em.

05:09.490 --> 05:11.150
If we can't defend
ourselves, you ought'a just

05:11.190 --> 05:13.320
serve us up on a platter.

05:13.360 --> 05:16.530
Why not let the two of us
withdraw from the front?

05:16.560 --> 05:17.860
Ymir!

05:17.900 --> 05:20.060
Negative. When we find
where they're coming in,

05:20.130 --> 05:22.230
I'll need someone
to relay it HQ.

05:22.300 --> 05:24.470
I know you're scared,
but like it or not,

05:24.500 --> 05:26.370
that's part of the job.

05:26.400 --> 05:28.400
[YMIR sighs]

05:32.310 --> 05:37.810
[CHRISTA] Ymir. Look, I'm aware
of what I've gotten myself into.

05:37.850 --> 05:40.020
Come on.
Hey, no one made me

05:40.050 --> 05:42.550
join the Scouts,
and you know it!

05:42.590 --> 05:46.990
I... I chose it for myself.

05:47.030 --> 05:49.330
I know it's a different
story in your case--

05:49.360 --> 05:51.430
What? Y'think I signed up
for all this crap

05:51.500 --> 05:52.900
because of you?

05:52.930 --> 05:55.500
What other reason do you
have for being here?

05:55.530 --> 05:57.870
You tried talking me into
joining the Military Police

05:57.900 --> 05:59.840
'til you were
blue in the face.

05:59.870 --> 06:02.770
You bowed out
so I'd be eligible!

06:02.840 --> 06:04.440
Don't try to deny it.

06:04.510 --> 06:06.940
I wasn't good enough to
make the top ten on my own.

06:07.010 --> 06:09.650
Ask anybody.
When it comes to skill,

06:09.680 --> 06:12.250
you're the better
soldier by far.

06:12.280 --> 06:16.720
I have no idea
how you did it, but...

06:16.760 --> 06:21.460
Why? Why do that for me?

06:24.600 --> 06:27.200
My family?

06:27.230 --> 06:29.870
That's it, isn't it?

06:31.800 --> 06:35.000
Sure. Why not?

06:36.510 --> 06:40.610
Relax. Don't worry
about it so much.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.750
Take my word for it, sweetie.

06:42.780 --> 06:46.120
I'm only lookin' out
for number one.

06:47.450 --> 06:50.350
[CHRISTA]
Really?

06:51.720 --> 06:54.690
That's such a relief.

07:07.470 --> 07:09.870
[MALE SOLDIER 28A] Steady!
The target is in range!

07:09.940 --> 07:13.740
[MALE SOLDIER 28B]
All cannons, prepare to fire!

07:13.780 --> 07:16.750
[KITZ]
Ready. Aim.

07:16.780 --> 07:18.480
[MALE SOLDIER 28C hollers]

07:18.520 --> 07:20.720
[KITZ]
Fire!

07:29.490 --> 07:31.660
[RICO grunts]

07:39.770 --> 07:41.600
That do the trick?

07:42.770 --> 07:44.610
[MALE SOLDIER 28D]
Nice one, Captain Rico!

07:44.640 --> 07:48.140
We keep this up they'll
never break our defense!

07:48.180 --> 07:49.650
[RICO]
Not necessarily.

07:49.680 --> 07:52.010
The enemy has
strength in numbers.

07:52.050 --> 07:54.220
If they attack en masse,
the line won't have

07:54.290 --> 07:57.650
a snowball's chance in hell.

07:57.690 --> 08:02.990
And worse, something's
off. Really off.

08:03.030 --> 08:04.730
[HANNES]
I don't like this.

08:04.800 --> 08:07.130
[PHIL] Captain Hannes,
sir. What's wrong?

08:07.170 --> 08:08.830
Anyone else
bothered by the fact

08:08.870 --> 08:11.370
we haven't spotted a Titan yet?

08:11.400 --> 08:14.840
You'd think the hole would've
jumped out at us by now.

08:14.870 --> 08:16.870
If where they're
getting in is nearby,

08:16.910 --> 08:19.710
why's it so quiet?

08:20.780 --> 08:22.980
Not that
I mind on principle.

08:23.010 --> 08:25.410
We find the damn thing and
get back without a scrape,

08:25.480 --> 08:27.650
all the better.

08:33.320 --> 08:48.140
[GELGAR breath deeply]

08:48.210 --> 08:54.080
[GELGAR] Please.
Just get it over with.

08:54.110 --> 08:56.680
I can't take this.

08:56.710 --> 09:00.620
Any second now they'll lunge
at us from the shadows.

09:02.050 --> 09:06.260
Dammit. The closer
we get to the entry point,

09:06.290 --> 09:07.920
the more it feels like
we're marching into

09:07.960 --> 09:10.390
the jaws of death.

09:10.430 --> 09:16.770
Ugh! This is driving
me out of my mind!

09:22.970 --> 09:25.410
[GELGAR gasps]

09:40.120 --> 09:42.960
So, you followed the
wall here too, I take it?

09:42.990 --> 09:46.200
That's right. I assume
you found the breach then?

09:46.230 --> 09:47.800
Huh?

09:47.830 --> 09:49.500
We didn't see
any irregularities

09:49.570 --> 09:51.500
along the western route.

09:51.570 --> 09:54.840
Surely you must've seen
something in the east?

09:54.910 --> 09:59.780
[GELGAR] No. The wall's
perfectly intact.

10:05.150 --> 10:07.280
Well, maybe we just
overlooked it?

10:07.320 --> 10:09.690
Not likely. Hole big
enough for Titans

10:09.750 --> 10:12.020
to get through? No way.

10:12.090 --> 10:14.590
I suggest we have
another pass, then.

10:14.630 --> 10:16.190
[NANABA]
That goes without saying.

10:16.260 --> 10:18.530
Trouble is, the horses
are on the verge of collapse

10:18.600 --> 10:20.860
and so are we.

10:20.930 --> 10:23.430
If only we had more light.

10:24.940 --> 10:27.300
[GELGAR]
Huh?

10:29.110 --> 10:31.540
What's that?

10:35.210 --> 10:38.180
[GELGAR] An old castle?

10:54.530 --> 10:56.230
[GELGAR] Not an ideal
place to sleep,

10:56.260 --> 10:59.660
but I guess we can make do
with it for one night.

10:59.700 --> 11:03.470
[NANABA] Yeah. And the moon's
finally out, at least.

11:11.880 --> 11:14.410
[LEVI]
Hey, Four-Eyes.

11:14.450 --> 11:17.750
Since when
are you a geologist?

11:17.780 --> 11:19.780
Or are rocks
just that fascinating?

11:19.850 --> 11:22.190
Looks like you're
about to drool.

11:22.220 --> 11:24.920
What, this?
It's not a rock.

11:24.960 --> 11:27.120
Not an ordinary one, anyway.

11:27.190 --> 11:31.290
It's a hardened piece of skin
left behind by the Female Titan.

11:31.360 --> 11:33.860
[Gasps]
It didn't vanish?

11:33.900 --> 11:36.370
No. This random
fragment broke off

11:36.400 --> 11:38.700
when Annie reverted
back to her human form.

11:38.740 --> 11:42.310
It didn't evaporate.
Didn't simply go "poof."

11:42.370 --> 11:43.910
So that got me thinking.

11:43.940 --> 11:46.080
And when I compared it
with a sliver of the wall,

11:46.110 --> 11:47.740
its texture
and composition were,

11:47.780 --> 11:51.110
for all intents and purposes,
virtually identical.

11:51.150 --> 11:52.650
In laymen's terms
we're hemmed in

11:52.720 --> 11:54.990
by a barricade
of enormous Titans.

11:55.050 --> 11:57.590
If my hypothesis is correct,
the surface was constructed

11:57.620 --> 12:00.590
using consolidated Titan skin.

12:00.630 --> 12:01.790
You're kidding me.

12:01.830 --> 12:04.130
That's what Armin
was trying to say.

12:04.160 --> 12:06.260
[Gasps]

12:06.300 --> 12:07.500
So, then--!

12:07.570 --> 12:10.070
Easy. It's rude to steal
someone else's thunder.

12:10.100 --> 12:12.440
As it stands, we'd be
hard-pressed to find a rock

12:12.470 --> 12:15.140
big enough to plug Wall Rose.

12:15.170 --> 12:17.470
It'd have to be just
the right shape and size,

12:17.510 --> 12:19.640
and we don't have specifics yet.

12:19.680 --> 12:21.310
[ARMIN and HANGE]
But, on the other hand,

12:21.380 --> 12:23.680
where there's
a will there's a way.

12:23.750 --> 12:26.120
Picture Eren utilizing
his hardening ability

12:26.190 --> 12:29.620
while in Titan form.

12:29.660 --> 12:35.590
I could... patch the hole.

12:35.630 --> 12:38.260
The sealant should be composed
of the same material.

12:38.300 --> 12:39.600
And the hardened bit
won't dissolve

12:39.670 --> 12:41.500
once you've transformed back.

12:41.530 --> 12:44.270
This might be less of
a long shot than it sounds.

12:44.300 --> 12:46.440
Thoughts?

12:48.970 --> 12:52.680
Well, anything worthwhile
incurs a little risk.

12:52.710 --> 12:55.550
If we can manage
to shore up Wall Rose,

12:55.610 --> 12:59.150
Wall Maria starts
to look fairly promising.

12:59.180 --> 13:01.790
Vital as it is,
the outpost infrastructure

13:01.820 --> 13:03.950
slows us down to a crawl.

13:03.990 --> 13:07.860
The time and resources needed to
transport materials are immense.

13:07.890 --> 13:11.230
But, if supply wagons don't
have to be accommodated,

13:11.300 --> 13:14.530
we can make our way to
Shiganshina much faster.

13:14.570 --> 13:16.470
And what if we decided
to carry out our plan

13:16.500 --> 13:17.900
in the dead of night?

13:17.970 --> 13:19.640
--[HANGE] Night?
--Yes.

13:19.670 --> 13:23.310
When the Titans
are effectively motionless.

13:23.340 --> 13:25.840
That's not bad.
In fact it's genius.

13:25.880 --> 13:27.540
Particularly if
the group is small enough

13:27.650 --> 13:30.880
to slip by undetected.

13:30.920 --> 13:33.880
The straits we're in
are as dire as they come.

13:33.920 --> 13:37.550
But there might just be
the teeniest bit of slack.

13:37.590 --> 13:40.090
Yeah. Just bear
in mind, though,

13:40.160 --> 13:41.730
the whole plan hinges
on whether or not

13:41.760 --> 13:43.860
Eren can seal a hole, again.

13:43.900 --> 13:45.700
[EREN gasps]

13:45.730 --> 13:49.600
It's, uh, probably
unfair of me to even ask.

13:49.670 --> 13:52.340
But do you think you can?

14:01.110 --> 14:04.610
[LEVI] What he thinks
really isn't the issue.

14:04.680 --> 14:07.880
You either will, or you won't.

14:07.920 --> 14:09.890
That's the reality.

14:09.920 --> 14:12.020
Our comrades are
breaking their backs,

14:12.060 --> 14:14.760
but without you, it's nothing.

14:14.790 --> 14:17.190
Failure isn't an option.

14:17.230 --> 14:18.960
Sir! I know!

14:19.030 --> 14:22.630
I'm prepared to do
whatever it takes!

14:22.700 --> 14:25.040
That's a promise.

14:31.240 --> 14:34.940
My father's cellar.
That's where the answers are.

14:34.980 --> 14:37.710
If there's a grain of
truth in what he told me,

14:37.750 --> 14:41.020
everything depends on
us making it there.

14:48.890 --> 14:51.130
[HANGE]
Here's Ehrmich.

15:02.070 --> 15:04.110
[Gasps]

15:04.140 --> 15:09.010
No one said stop. A rolling
stone gathers no moss.

15:09.080 --> 15:10.480
This is...

15:10.520 --> 15:14.080
Maybe you expected
to see something quaint?

15:14.120 --> 15:17.190
This is what happens
when the walls give.

15:17.260 --> 15:22.560
[BOY 28A sobs]
Mommy! Daddy!

15:22.630 --> 15:23.990
[Gasps]

15:24.030 --> 15:28.160
[LEVI]
No. Take it in, holy man.

15:28.200 --> 15:30.100
These are the faces
of human beings

15:30.140 --> 15:33.440
who've lost everything
they ever had.

15:33.470 --> 15:37.270
Human beings you and your
kind abandoned, incidentally.

15:37.310 --> 15:39.510
Hard to look at it, I'd imagine.

15:39.540 --> 15:43.050
But if the church had its way,
this'd be all of us.

15:43.120 --> 15:45.680
Titans would pour in and
make a feast of what's left.

15:45.780 --> 15:49.690
Shoveling man, woman, and child
down their putrescent gullets.

15:49.720 --> 15:53.460
All humanity
digested as one.

15:56.130 --> 15:57.530
[HANGE]
Once we leave Ehrmich,

15:57.560 --> 16:00.200
we'll be in
Titan territory proper.

16:00.230 --> 16:02.800
Eren. Well enough
to ride a horse yet?

16:02.830 --> 16:04.400
[EREN] Yeah, should be
able to manage one

16:04.470 --> 16:06.000
without much of a hassle.

16:06.040 --> 16:07.340
Saddle up then, soldier.

16:07.370 --> 16:09.310
There's a mount waiting
for you on the left lift.

16:09.340 --> 16:11.140
[EREN]
Right.

16:12.910 --> 16:15.150
Section Commander,
we're pressed for time.

16:15.180 --> 16:18.980
Oh. Thanks, Moblit.
Give me a sec.

16:19.020 --> 16:22.850
So? Seen the light yet,
by any chance?

16:26.930 --> 16:29.360
Oh, goddamn it!
Make up your mind!

16:29.390 --> 16:34.060
This isn't some spiritual test!
Lives are on the line!

16:34.100 --> 16:36.370
Alas, I have no choice.

16:36.400 --> 16:38.500
Neither myself nor
the others who believe

16:38.540 --> 16:41.200
are at liberty
to divulge the truth.

16:41.240 --> 16:43.240
Fat lot a help you are!

16:43.280 --> 16:46.910
Thanks for keeping us company!
It's been fun!

16:46.950 --> 16:48.780
[NICK] I'd offer
my help if I could,

16:48.850 --> 16:52.720
but a duty as great
as this one is beyond me.

16:52.750 --> 16:55.620
The Order of the Walls
abides by the sacred will

16:55.690 --> 16:58.190
--our faith commands us to obey.
--[GIRL] Sir! Thank you, sir!

16:58.220 --> 17:00.060
Whose "sacred will"?

17:00.090 --> 17:02.030
You mean like God,
or something?

17:02.060 --> 17:05.700
I can't answer that.
But what I can do

17:05.730 --> 17:07.930
is provide you with a name.

17:07.970 --> 17:10.370
An individual the sacred will
in its divine wisdom

17:10.400 --> 17:12.570
instructed us to monitor.

17:12.600 --> 17:15.570
Monitor?

17:15.610 --> 17:17.140
It's a person you know.

17:17.210 --> 17:20.040
Someone who enlisted with the
Scout Regiment as of this year.

17:20.080 --> 17:22.480
[ALL gasp]

17:22.550 --> 17:24.610
A child by the name of...

17:24.680 --> 17:26.120
[SASHA]
Important message!

17:26.220 --> 17:28.080
I'm with the 104th Cadet Corps!

17:28.120 --> 17:30.450
Oh, and my name
is Sasha Braus!

17:30.520 --> 17:31.320
[Gasps]

17:31.390 --> 17:33.660
[Gasps]
No way.

17:33.730 --> 17:34.920
Who?

17:34.960 --> 17:37.490
Sorry. This is for you,
Section Commander.

17:37.560 --> 17:41.560
You must find her with
all haste. She is the key.

17:41.600 --> 17:45.300
She may know things
we understand but poorly.

17:45.340 --> 17:46.970
And with that,
we come to the end

17:47.010 --> 17:48.610
of what I'm free to share.

17:48.640 --> 17:50.110
[Inhales]

17:50.140 --> 17:53.010
The rest I leave
in your capable hands.

17:53.080 --> 17:55.480
But if, if she's in
the 104th Cadet Corps,

17:55.510 --> 17:57.110
she's at the front lines by now!

17:57.150 --> 18:00.020
Then let's go! Come on!
There's no time to lose!

18:00.090 --> 18:00.920
[SASHA groans]

18:00.950 --> 18:03.250
Watch where you're going!

18:03.290 --> 18:04.790
Sasha?

18:04.820 --> 18:09.690
Just where did you
come from all of a sudden?

18:09.760 --> 18:13.100
I was sent to give a message
to Commander Erwin.

18:13.130 --> 18:14.600
Who, then, entrusted me
to deliver this

18:14.630 --> 18:17.270
to you,
Section Commander!

18:17.300 --> 18:22.040
Oh, uh. Okay, then.
Excellent work.

18:23.010 --> 18:24.140
[Gasps]

18:24.180 --> 18:26.810
[HANGE] So, who is
Nick talking about?

18:26.850 --> 18:29.380
She was the smallest
one in our class.

18:29.450 --> 18:31.680
Golden hair. Blue eyes.

18:31.720 --> 18:36.250
In fact, she's,
uh, kinda cute.

18:37.790 --> 18:41.060
The girl who's always
hanging around Ymir.

18:41.130 --> 18:43.430
Excuse me?

18:45.730 --> 18:49.170
[REINER]
How can you read this?

18:49.200 --> 18:53.900
Ymir. Do you?

18:55.470 --> 18:59.980
Everyone, wake up!
Get to the tower immediately!

19:08.350 --> 19:10.150
[LYNNE] I couldn't
see them in the dark,

19:10.190 --> 19:12.490
but with the moonlight...

19:14.030 --> 19:17.030
How can they move?
This shouldn't be happening!

19:17.060 --> 19:19.700
The sun went down hours ago!

19:21.000 --> 19:22.830
Wh-What's going on?

19:22.870 --> 19:26.540
Hey, guys.
The hell is that?

19:26.570 --> 19:28.400
It's gotta be a Titan,

19:28.440 --> 19:30.940
but have you ever
seen one that big?

19:31.010 --> 19:35.580
Look at it! It's more like,
some kind of beast.

19:35.610 --> 19:37.550
How do we--?

19:40.850 --> 19:44.750
Wait, is it?
It's headed for the wall!

19:50.560 --> 19:52.300
That's the plan.
Are we clear?

19:52.360 --> 19:53.630
[ALL]
Yes, clear!

19:53.700 --> 19:55.900
Right. We have to go! Now!

19:55.930 --> 19:57.900
[LEVI]
Calm down, Eren.

19:59.200 --> 20:01.200
I need you all to listen.

20:01.240 --> 20:05.110
We're going our separate ways.
That's how it has to be.

20:05.140 --> 20:06.740
Erwin had his reasons
for throwing this

20:06.780 --> 20:11.110
ragtag squad together, but right
now this is all riding on you.

20:11.150 --> 20:13.420
Armin, you and Hange
are the brain trust.

20:13.450 --> 20:16.490
Use your combined knowledge to
cook up some kind of solution.

20:16.550 --> 20:18.290
Right. Yes, sir!

20:18.320 --> 20:21.320
Mikasa. I don't think
I'll ever get why

20:21.390 --> 20:23.430
you're so attached
to the guy, but,

20:23.460 --> 20:27.300
put your skills to good use.
Protect Eren at all costs.

20:27.330 --> 20:30.170
Sir! I intend to!

20:30.240 --> 20:34.440
[LEVI] And you.
Don't screw this up.

20:37.810 --> 20:41.910
Hey, hey! Back off!
Don't be coming up here!

20:43.280 --> 20:45.750
Ain't'cha got
nothin' better to do?

20:45.820 --> 20:47.620
Bother someone else.

20:47.650 --> 20:49.590
I should be drinking
right now, damn it!

20:49.620 --> 20:52.520
You're standing between me
and a tankard of ale!

20:52.590 --> 20:54.920
I've earned the right
to get trashed!

20:54.960 --> 20:57.630
[NANABA] Rookies!
Stay where you are!

20:57.660 --> 20:59.860
We've got this.

20:59.930 --> 21:03.330
Let the ODM gear do
what it was designed for.

21:05.070 --> 21:08.340
Attack!

21:08.370 --> 21:18.350
♪

21:24.220 --> 21:26.460
[LEVI]
Check your emotions, Eren.

21:26.490 --> 21:29.330
Learn the meaning
of the word restraint.

21:29.360 --> 21:33.330
If you let yourself succumb to
blind rage, all hope is lost.

21:33.400 --> 21:35.970
We can't afford another mistake.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.000
Sir!

21:39.740 --> 21:40.900
[HANGE]
There's a tower nearby

21:40.970 --> 21:43.170
that'll give us
access to the wall.

21:43.210 --> 21:46.540
Part of an abandoned
fortification to the southwest.

21:46.580 --> 21:49.880
We ride with all haste
for Utgard Castle!

21:51.050 --> 22:01.020
[Intense music plays]

22:10.170 --> 22:15.170
♪ Closing Song
